  "description": "KADNUC crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C71 H86 Eu5 N12 O30,3(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.666-3.935 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.53-115.20°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C74H97Eu5N12O33.",
